  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3.75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using the expansion, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />For limit to exist numerator &amp; denominator must be of the same degree<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Also,&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />By equations <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.75</mo></math></p>",
